#: src/pages/ImageCompressPage.tsx:175
msgid "Yes, compression involves a trade-off between file size and quality. Smaller targets require more aggressive compression. For best results, choose the largest target size that meets your requirements."
msgstr "Yes, compression involves a trade-off between file size and quality. Smaller targets require more aggressive compression. For best results, choose the largest target size that meets your requirements."

#: src/pages/VideoCompressPage.tsx:261
msgid "Yes, some quality loss is expected. High quality mode preserves most detail. Medium is a good balance. Low prioritizes small file size over visual quality."
msgstr "Yes, some quality loss is expected. High quality mode preserves most detail. Medium is a good balance. Low prioritizes small file size over visual quality."

#: src/pages/DecompressPage.tsx:100
msgid "Yes. After extraction you can download files one at a time, or download all extracted files bundled as a single ZIP."
msgstr "Yes. After extraction you can download files one at a time, or download all extracted files bundled as a single ZIP."

#: src/pages/ImageToPdfPage.tsx:105
msgid "Yes. After uploading your images, you can drag and drop them to rearrange the order. Each image becomes one page in the final PDF."
msgstr "Yes. After uploading your images, you can drag and drop them to rearrange the order. Each image becomes one page in the final PDF."

#: src/pages/VideoGifPage.tsx:367
msgid "Yes. After uploading, a video player lets you preview your file. The clip range slider shows exactly which segment will be converted."
msgstr "Yes. After uploading, a video player lets you preview your file. The clip range slider shows exactly which segment will be converted."

#: src/pages/PdfEditorPage.tsx:864
msgid "Yes. All editing features can be combined in a single operation — rotate, reorder, watermark, page numbers, and redactions are applied together."
msgstr "Yes. All editing features can be combined in a single operation — rotate, reorder, watermark, page numbers, and redactions are applied together."

#: src/pages/CertConvertPage.tsx:176
msgid "Yes. All intermediate and root certificates present in the source file are included in the converted output."
msgstr "Yes. All intermediate and root certificates present in the source file are included in the converted output."

#: src/pages/YamlJsonPage.tsx:736
msgid "Yes. Click the \"Sort keys\" button in the toolbar to recursively sort all object keys in alphabetical order in both the YAML and JSON output."
msgstr "Yes. Click the \"Sort keys\" button in the toolbar to recursively sort all object keys in alphabetical order in both the YAML and JSON output."

#: src/pages/JsonCsvPage.tsx:461
msgid "Yes. Dynamic typing is enabled by default, so numeric strings become numbers, \"true\"/\"false\" become booleans, and empty cells become null."
msgstr "Yes. Dynamic typing is enabled by default, so numeric strings become numbers, \"true\"/\"false\" become booleans, and empty cells become null."

#: src/pages/DecompressPage.tsx:98
msgid "Yes. Enter the password in the optional password field before uploading the file."
msgstr "Yes. Enter the password in the optional password field before uploading the file."

#: src/pages/HashGeneratorPage.tsx:552
msgid "Yes. Files are read in 2 MB chunks, so memory usage stays low regardless of file size. However, very large files (several GB) will take longer to process."
msgstr "Yes. Files are read in 2 MB chunks, so memory usage stays low regardless of file size. However, very large files (several GB) will take longer to process."

#: src/pages/YamlJsonPage.tsx:733
msgid "Yes. If your YAML contains multiple documents separated by ---, they are parsed individually and merged into a JSON array."
msgstr "Yes. If your YAML contains multiple documents separated by ---, they are parsed individually and merged into a JSON array."

#: src/pages/PasswordGeneratorPage.tsx:530
msgid "Yes. It uses the Web Crypto API (crypto.getRandomValues) which provides cryptographically secure random numbers. However, for long-term credential management, a dedicated password manager is always recommended."
msgstr "Yes. It uses the Web Crypto API (crypto.getRandomValues) which provides cryptographically secure random numbers. However, for long-term credential management, a dedicated password manager is always recommended."

#: src/pages/CertInspectPage.tsx:796
msgid "Yes. P12 and PFX files that require a password will prompt you to enter it before analysis."
msgstr "Yes. P12 and PFX files that require a password will prompt you to enter it before analysis."

#: src/pages/PdfMergePage.tsx:106
msgid "Yes. Pages appear in the merged PDF in the same order you arrange them. Use drag-and-drop to reorder files before merging."
msgstr "Yes. Pages appear in the merged PDF in the same order you arrange them. Use drag-and-drop to reorder files before merging."

#: src/pages/EbookConvertPage.tsx:119
msgid "Yes. PDF to EPUB conversion works best with text-based PDFs. Scanned/image-only PDFs may produce limited results since there is no OCR step."
msgstr "Yes. PDF to EPUB conversion works best with text-based PDFs. Scanned/image-only PDFs may produce limited results since there is no OCR step."

#: src/pages/PdfEditorPage.tsx:863
msgid "Yes. Redacted areas are permanently removed from the PDF at the server level. The content cannot be recovered or revealed."
msgstr "Yes. Redacted areas are permanently removed from the PDF at the server level. The content cannot be recovered or revealed."

#: src/pages/PdfExtractImagesPage.tsx:123
msgid "Yes. Scanned PDFs typically contain one large image per page, and each page image will be extracted."
msgstr "Yes. Scanned PDFs typically contain one large image per page, and each page image will be extracted."

#: src/pages/ImageConvertPage.tsx:890
msgid "Yes. SVG vector files are rasterized to PNG. You can optionally specify an output width — height scales proportionally to maintain the aspect ratio."
msgstr "Yes. SVG vector files are rasterized to PNG. You can optionally specify an output width — height scales proportionally to maintain the aspect ratio."

#: src/pages/MarkdownPdfPage.tsx:154
msgid "Yes. Switch to the \"Paste markdown\" tab to type or paste your content directly. The conversion works the same way."
msgstr "Yes. Switch to the \"Paste markdown\" tab to type or paste your content directly. The conversion works the same way."

#: src/pages/EbookConvertPage.tsx:122
msgid "Yes. The converter preserves images, table of contents, chapter structure, and text formatting whenever the target format supports them."
msgstr "Yes. The converter preserves images, table of contents, chapter structure, and text formatting whenever the target format supports them."

#: src/pages/WordCounterPage.tsx:149
msgid "Yes. The word counter works with any language that uses whitespace to separate words, including most European languages. For CJK languages without word boundaries, the character count is more useful."
msgstr "Yes. The word counter works with any language that uses whitespace to separate words, including most European languages. For CJK languages without word boundaries, the character count is more useful."

#: src/pages/OcrPage.tsx:353
msgid "Yes. Upload the PDF and the OCR engine will analyze the scanned pages and extract any readable text."
msgstr "Yes. Upload the PDF and the OCR engine will analyze the scanned pages and extract any readable text."

#: src/pages/PdfEditorPage.tsx:862
msgid "Yes. Use the Reset button on the Pages tab to restore the original page order and rotations. You can also start over at any time."
msgstr "Yes. Use the Reset button on the Pages tab to restore the original page order and rotations. You can also start over at any time."

#: src/pages/FontConvertPage.tsx:115
msgid "Yes. Variable font axes and instances are preserved during conversion between compatible formats."
msgstr "Yes. Variable font axes and instances are preserved during conversion between compatible formats."

#: src/pages/QrCodePage.tsx:405
msgid "Yes. You can change foreground/background colors, dot shape (square, circle, liquid), and eye shape (square, rounded)."
msgstr "Yes. You can change foreground/background colors, dot shape (square, circle, liquid), and eye shape (square, rounded)."

#: src/pages/PdfMergePage.tsx:105
msgid "Yes. You can combine PDF files with JPG, PNG, WebP, BMP, and TIFF images. Each image is converted to a PDF page during the merge."
msgstr "Yes. You can combine PDF files with JPG, PNG, WebP, BMP, and TIFF images. Each image is converted to a PDF page during the merge."

#: src/pages/ImageToPdfPage.tsx:103
msgid "You can combine up to 10 images into a single PDF. Each image can be up to 8 MB in size."
msgstr "You can combine up to 10 images into a single PDF. Each image can be up to 8 MB in size."

#: src/pages/FontConvertPage.tsx:111
msgid "You can convert between TTF (TrueType), OTF (OpenType), WOFF, and WOFF2. Any input format can be converted to any output format."
msgstr "You can convert between TTF (TrueType), OTF (OpenType), WOFF, and WOFF2. Any input format can be converted to any output format."

#: src/pages/CertConvertPage.tsx:174
msgid "You can convert from PEM, CRT, CER, DER, P12/PFX, and P7B/P7C to any of the four target formats: PEM, DER, PKCS#12, and PKCS#7."
msgstr "You can convert from PEM, CRT, CER, DER, P12/PFX, and P7B/P7C to any of the four target formats: PEM, DER, PKCS#12, and PKCS#7."

#: src/pages/ArchivePage.tsx:186
msgid "You can create ZIP, 7z, tar.gz (gzip compressed), and tar.zst (Zstandard compressed) archives."
msgstr "You can create ZIP, 7z, tar.gz (gzip compressed), and tar.zst (Zstandard compressed) archives."

#: src/pages/QrCodePage.tsx:402
msgid "You can encode any text or URL (up to 4,096 characters) or WiFi network credentials including SSID, password, encryption type, and hidden network flag."
msgstr "You can encode any text or URL (up to 4,096 characters) or WiFi network credentials including SSID, password, encryption type, and hidden network flag."

#: src/pages/PdfMergePage.tsx:104
msgid "You can merge up to 10 files in a single operation. Each file can be up to 8 MB."
msgstr "You can merge up to 10 files in a single operation. Each file can be up to 8 MB."

#: src/pages/VideoGifPage.tsx:364
msgid "You can select a clip up to 15 seconds long. Shorter clips produce smaller, more shareable GIFs."
msgstr "You can select a clip up to 15 seconds long. Shorter clips produce smaller, more shareable GIFs."

#: src/pages/PdfEditorPage.tsx:861
msgid "You can upload PDF files up to 100 MB. The editor renders page thumbnails locally in your browser for fast interaction."
msgstr "You can upload PDF files up to 100 MB. The editor renders page thumbnails locally in your browser for fast interaction."

#: src/pages/PdfRepairPage.tsx:92
msgid "You can upload PDF files up to 20 MB for repair."
msgstr "You can upload PDF files up to 20 MB for repair."

#: src/pages/SecurityPage.tsx:41
msgid "Your file is sent over TLS and stored in volatile memory (RAM). It never touches a physical disk."
msgstr "Your file is sent over TLS and stored in volatile memory (RAM). It never touches a physical disk."

#: src/pages/HomePage.tsx:78
msgid "Your files stay yours — never stored"
msgstr "Your files stay yours — never stored"

#: src/pages/AsciiPage.tsx:410
msgid "Your image never leaves your browser. All conversion happens locally using the Canvas API."
msgstr "Your image never leaves your browser. All conversion happens locally using the Canvas API."

#: src/pages/ImageConvertPage.tsx:646
msgid "Your watermark text"
msgstr "Your watermark text"

#: src/pages/ArchivePage.tsx:187
msgid "ZIP and 7z support AES-256 password encryption. Tar-based formats (tar.gz, tar.zst) do not support built-in encryption."
msgstr "ZIP and 7z support AES-256 password encryption. Tar-based formats (tar.gz, tar.zst) do not support built-in encryption."

